# No internal doc refs on user-facing surfaces

Traces to `[Corpus: product §F7]` / `[Corpus: product §F21]` / EV-048 (#951) /
`D-S057-*` guards. Planning vocabulary belongs in agent/docs/tests — **never** in
operator or public surfaces.

## Forbidden tokens (operator / public)

Do not put these in UI copy, OpenAPI descriptions/summaries/examples, HTTP
`detail` / error bodies, toasts, help text, lint `source_attribution`, or any
string an operator or anonymous client can see:

| Pattern | Examples |
|---------|----------|
| Corpus cites | `[Corpus: product]`, `[Corpus: api]` |
| Doc paths | `docs/sessions/…`, `docs/feature-list` |
| ADRs / evolve / sessions | `ADR-022`, `EV-048`, `S057` |
| Test / interview ids | `TC-F7-002`, `E11-31`, `UJ-016` |
| Issue / feature shorthand | `#702`, `F21`, `F7.g` |

## Allowed

- Code comments, module docstrings, tests, ADRs, session reports, commit/PR text
- Agent replies that cite `[Corpus: …]` for design gates
- Stable **domain** codes operators already use (`INVALID_RVR`, product names)

## Do

- Write plain-language operator copy (see Soft-preview help after EV-048).
- Keep provenance `note` / attribution free of planning ids; put tickets in
  `ticket` / digs only (`PROVENANCE_MAP.json`).
- Extend BE OpenAPI + FE `internalDocRefGuard` / `operatorVisibleCopy` when adding
  new public string catalogs.
- Prefer scrubbing at the source (copy, OpenAPI, provenance) over allowlists.

## Do not

- “Trace to ADR-0xx” inside Form/Field descriptions or FE labels.
- Embed `EV-` / `#NNN` in lint catalog attribution notes that join into
  `source_attribution` (served via `/lint-issue-catalog`).
- Waive by stuffing cites into tooltips, `aria-label`, or example TAC labels.

Guards: `apps/backend/tests/unit/test_tc_ev048_openapi_internal_doc_refs.py`,
`apps/frontend/src/utils/internalDocRefGuard.ts`.
